WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:03.520
Let's briefly talk about Unreal Engine

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.099
as it applies to game development.

3
00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:09.640
Unreal Engine has always fundamentally been a game

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.519
engine, allows you to create content,

5
00:00:12.519 --> 00:00:15.320
let players move around and interact with it,

6
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.800
and ultimately allow this dynamic exchange

7
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.399
between what the player wants to do and an experience

8
00:00:20.399 --> 00:00:23.070
that you create for them.

9
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.829
There are many benefits to using Unreal Engine for game

10
00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:26.949
development.

11
00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:29.289
But as it pertains to Sequencer,

12
00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:30.949
the most important thing to remember

13
00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:33.890
is that we are building this world for the players

14
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.030
to interact with and then occasionally stepping

15
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.509
in to present them with a visual experience

16
00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:43.229
or a montage of images, sound, et cetera.

17
00:00:43.229 --> 00:00:47.609
And we do that predominantly through Sequencer.

18
00:00:47.609 --> 00:00:49.250
One of the important things that we

19
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:52.890
want to discuss as we go throughout this course

20
00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.770
is the concept of how games are made, released,

21
00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:59.090
and content patched into it.

22
00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:02.689
So throughout this process of building our sequence,

23
00:01:02.689 --> 00:01:06.409
you'll find that we will do certain practices to keep

24
00:01:06.409 --> 00:01:10.219
good organization and structure, keeping in mind that typically

25
00:01:10.219 --> 00:01:12.299
during a video game, you're going

26
00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:15.420
to have several cinematic experiences, meaning

27
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:20.219
you want to have a very strong, flexible, and adaptable

28
00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:24.019
pipeline and process for building your sequences

29
00:01:24.019 --> 00:01:28.140
and running them or executing them in the final game.
